  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book is silkscreen and digitally printed on Mohawk Superfine 65# cover stock. Hand bound by Lisa Hersey in Easthampton, Massachusetts."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The images on the end sheets are hate symbols listed on the Anti-Defamation League database"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Inspired by the rise in ultra-nationalism and worldwide threat to the democratic ideas and principles Your Leader Could be a Tyrant, How to Tell incorporates silhouetted images of each tyrant with hand stamped text about their peculiar habits, statistical information about their rule with accompanying texts discussing common traits of dictators. Originally conceived as a companion to Your Co-Worker Could Be A Space Alien from 1985, this book mixes humor and horror to underscore our contemporary reality."-- https://wsworkshop.org/collection/your-leader-could-be-a-tyrant-how-to-tell/ (viewed Dec. 4, 2019).</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes answer key, "The Freedom House survey, 2019 : countries ruled by a dictator or strongman"--Pages 60-61.</subfield>
  </datafield>
